Z||000044||LZeitgeist||07-17-2001||09:39 AM||||Skitime, could you please make a 'How-To' on how you put the clear panel in the decklid? I've been wanting to do that ever since I got my first V6 Fiero... it will be going into a notchback decklid, though, instead of the fastback like yours...<P>Pleeeeeease?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000045||LZeitgeist||07-18-2001||08:36 AM||||*bump*<P>Pleeeeeeeease?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000046||skitime||07-18-2001||09:15 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LZeitgeist:<BR><B>Skitime, could you please make a 'How-To' on how you put the clear panel in the decklid? I've been wanting to do that ever since I got my first V6 Fiero... it will be going into a notchback decklid, though, instead of the fastback like yours...<P>Pleeeeeease?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well I didn't take any pictures but it is pretty straightforward.  I worked with a scrap trunk to get my ideas worked out. I tried several different methods of installing the glass. Currently it is Lexan but I am having a tempered glass made. There are three ways of mounting:Below(easiest) Dado Joint (Tricky making the glass with a dado), Flush (hardest but what I thought would look the best).  I made all three types to see which I wanted. I did my cutting with a router. (wear breathing protection).  I cut the lexan to rough size and sanded until I had a good friction fit. I used some silicon to seal it but the tight fit is really holding it in place.  The panel is not flat even though it appear to be. That really added difficulty in getting glass made. I think the notchback trunk is not as flat which would add new challenges.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000047||LZeitgeist||07-18-2001||08:51 PM||||Man, sounds like a helluva job.. thanks for the advice - yours looks AMAZING!!!||||reg||1
Z||000048||AusFiero||07-20-2001||09:02 PM||||Yep that is one sweet car Skitime. I also thought about rear deck louvers of kinds and a window. I was thinking V8 under it though with 4 dual barrel downdraft webber carbies with chrome trumpets. Mega dollars though. Hope I get to check your car out in person when I come stateside next year. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000049||skitime||07-20-2001||09:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B>Yep that is one sweet car Skitime. I also thought about rear deck louvers of kinds and a window. I was thinking V8 under it though with 4 dual barrel downdraft webber carbies with chrome trumpets. Mega dollars though. Hope I get to check your car out in person when I come stateside next year. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks AusFiero coming from you that is quite a compliment. I would love to meet you and have you check this car out. Be sure to let me know when you come to the states. We could even put a roof over your head while you are here. I got the idea from the 2001 Ferrari spyder 360 which actually I saw in a magazine I was looking at on the bus ride to buy my t-top.  I was thinking how cool it be to look at a 3800 supercharger. <BR>||||reg||1
